  "details": "The “VeryPoor” performance rank is no longer a reliable indicator, and hiding it would make most current avatars in the Japanese community unviewable.\n\nFurthermore, an increasing number of low-capacity avatars have been created solely by recklessly reducing texture memory without addressing rendering load. These avatars exceed CPU and GPU processing limits, causing frame drops even when the number of displayed users is drastically reduced.\n\nTherefore, we need a feature to force hide avatars with one or more abnormally high performance metrics unless the player chooses to display them. This aligns with measures against disruptive behavior in VRChat.",
